index 3cd7f37..25675a0 100644
--- a/patches/README.md
+++ b/patches/README.md
@@ -315,3 +315,4 @@ Reserved:
   0180 brings TenSeven's Calendar and Phone extras into the Sable apps (owner, 2026-11-12): Sable Calendar's busy rings split by calendar, each calendar's arc in its own colour and sharing the day's sweep (`CalendarBusy.arcs`, unit-tested); a Day view (V cycles Agenda, Day, Week, Month) with the day's timeline, NOW line and arrows to step a day; a line under Add account naming DAVx⁵ for Google, iCloud and Yahoo and ICSx⁵ for an Outlook link. Sable Phone's Calls, Favorites and Contacts rows show the contact's photo, or initials on a disc (`Avatar.initials`, unit-tested); hidden and private callers show `#`.
   0181 ships the calendar account apps the owner chose (2026-11-12, "Ship both, pinned"): DAVx⁵ (`sable-src/apps/r8/davx5`, v4.5.21-ose) for Google, iCloud and Yahoo calendars and ICSx⁵ (`sable-src/apps/r8/icsx5`, v2.4.3) for calendar links such as Outlook's, built from pinned source with only the release signing removed and the Sable launcher icon (Phosphor `arrows-clockwise` and `link-simple`, generated). Sable Mail's flavor takes an owner Microsoft client (`SABLE_MAIL_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID`, `SABLE_MAIL_MICROSOFT_SIGNATURE_HASH`) next to Gmail's, with the `msauth://` redirect the verifier requires. Cosgrove's texting guards `SmsManager.createForSubscriptionId` (API 31) for its minSdk 30.
   0182 brings email into the Hub (owner, 2026-11-12: Hub email in 2.0, "just Sable Mail for sable os"): Sable Mail is back in the image; its flavor adds `SableMailHubProvider` (`content://org.sableos.mail.hub/messages`, the 50 newest Inbox headers across accounts, read-only, only for the SableOS home and Sable Hub, change-notified from Thunderbird's message list) and `SableMailOpenActivity` (`org.sableos.mail.action.OPEN_MESSAGE`). The home flavor's `patch_hub_mail` adds `SableMailFeed.kt` (unit-tested), which lists those messages in the Hub in place of Sable Mail's notifications and opens one in Sable Mail; `verify_sable_tenseven.py` checks it (`hub_mail`).
+  0183 gives the upstream apps the BlackBerry look (owner, 2026-11-12: every SableOS app in the BlackBerry theme): DAVx⁵, ICSx⁵ and Sable Terminal (ConnectBot) replace their Material 3 colour schemes with the Sable colours, one table shared by the three flavors (black, white and #2E9BD6; raised #141414, dividers #262626; light: #1A6FA0 on #F5F7F9), and Terminal stops taking Android's wallpaper colours.
